{
  "notes": [
    "TODO(spike): the `ruleGroup` format is not documented by the blocks-data-gateway-configuration skill or the CLI (the CLI passes it through untouched). The ruleGroups below are INTENT NOTATION and must be translated to the real Data Gateway syntax after the Phase 2 spike, before `blocks data rules deploy` / `blocks data sync` is run with --yes.",
    "Intent notation: a group is {combinator: and|or, rules: [...]}; a rule is {field, operator: equals|in, value} where value may be $currentUser.userId, $currentUser.organizationIds, or $currentUser.organizationIdsWithRole:<role>; {currentUserRole: <role>} matches a global role.",
    "Every schema except ModelPrice READ is accessLevel 3 (Custom), so anything without an allow policy is denied to browser users. WRITE/EDIT/DELETE on UsageEvent, UserHourly, TeamHourly and IngestKey deliberately have no allow policies: only workflows write them.",
    "TODO(spike): which identity workflows (dataAction with blocksAuthentication) act as, and whether Custom security without allow policies also blocks them. If it does, add a role/identity-scoped allow policy for the workflow identity on those operations.",
    "TODO(spike): per-organization roles. $currentUser.organizationIdsWithRole:team-admin assumes Blocks can match a row field against the organizations where the viewer holds a role. If it can't, fall back to: team-admin views served by a blocksAuthorization workflow that checks the role, and rows readable only by owner + platform-admin.",
    "TODO(spike): CLS on promptPreview must hide the column from team-admin and platform-admin as well. If CLS can't be row-conditional (owner of THAT row), move previews into a separate UsagePreview schema (eventId, userId, preview) with owner-only RLS, and drop promptPreview from UsageEvent."
  ],
